  "description": "Word order and particles for emphasis",
  "descriptionRussian": "Порядок слов и частицы для выделения",
  "imageName": "exclamationmark.circle",
  "intro": "Russian uses several strategies for emphasis. WORD ORDER: Move emphasized element to end or beginning: Книгу я прочитал (I DID read the book). PARTICLES: же (emphasis), -то (contrast), именно (specifically), как раз (exactly). INTONATION: Stress shifts meaning. CLEFT CONSTRUCTIONS: Это он сделал (It was HE who did it). Unlike English 'do'-emphasis, Russian relies on position and particles. New/important information naturally goes last (rheme position).",
  "rules": [
    "End position = new/emphasized: Книгу я прочитал (the BOOK I read)",
    "Particles: же (strong), -то (contrast), именно (specifically), как раз (exactly)",
    "Cleft for focus: Это я виноват (It's I who am guilty)",
    "Beginning position can emphasize topic: Эту книгу я уже читал (THIS book I've read)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Вчера же я тебе сказал! (I told you YESTERDAY!)",
    "Он-то знает правду. (HE knows the truth, unlike others.)",
    "Именно это я имел в виду. (That's EXACTLY what I meant.)",
    "Книгу он так и не прочитал. (The book he never DID read.)"
  ],
